  "question": {
    "text": "A long wire carries a steady current. It is bent into a circle of one turn and the magnetic field at the center of the coil is <math><mi>B</mi></math>. It is then bent into a circular loop of <math><mi>n</mi></math> turns. The magnetic field at the centre of coil will be"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math><mi>n</mi><mi>B</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>B</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi><mi>B</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mi>B</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Suppose the length of wire is <math><mi>l</mi></math><br /><br />Then, for the circle of n turns<br /><br />The magnetic field, <math> <mrow> <mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac> <mrow> <msub> <mi>μ</mi> <mn>0</mn> </msub> <mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi></mrow> <mrow> <mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math> , where R is the radius of the circle<br /><br />Then <math><msub><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> =B......(i)<br /><br />Here, <math><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>l</mi></math> .......(ii)<br /><br />Now, if the same wire is turned into a coil of n turns of radius a then,<br /><br /><math><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>l</mi></math> .......(iii)<br /><br />Thus, <math><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>×</mo><mi>n</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />Now, the magnetic field for the coil of n turns, is<br /><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi>B</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mi>n</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mi>I</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mo>∵</mo><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>B</mi></math>"
  }
